Injecting closures is inferior to injecting a real type or even calling a parent method, spreading the opposite would be defeating decades of software design culture, not revolutionizing. I don't think we want developing with Symfony to be injecting PHPDoc-typed closures everywhere. I'm against spreading that practice as a best one to our users as it'd be pushing for poorly designed and hard to apprehend code that misses leveraging language type capabilities.
